<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28072" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Măro</span></b> , ōnis,
			m.
		from root smar-, to be thoughtful; cf. memor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the family name of the
				poet</i> P. Vergilius, <i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 15,
			12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingenium sacri miraris abesse Maronis: Sint
					Maecenates, non deerunt, Flacce, Marones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					8, 56, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">summus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 4, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">altisonus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					11, 180</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a
				statue of Virgil</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 7, 227</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mă-rōnēus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the poet Virgil, Maronian, Virgilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 4, 55</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mărōnĭā-nus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., Maronian,
			Virgilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">culex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 2, 7, 74</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stilus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 1</span></i>
			
			<i>in carm</i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
